@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] hosted-server-is-the-rust-server-in-a-worker
The hosted server MUST be the Rust server in `backend/` built for Workers, answering every request
through its own router (`transport::router`) inside the `PullyServer` Durable Object. Server
behaviour MUST NOT be reimplemented in this crate or in JavaScript; this crate only connects the
server to the Worker runtime: requests, environment and storage (Tavi, 24 Oct 2026, "Rewrite it as
a Worker"; `plans/12-hosted-server.md`, Update 24 Oct).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] hosted-server-only-behind-access
The Worker MUST NOT have a `workers.dev` or preview URL. A route or custom domain MUST be added only
together with the Cloudflare Access policy in front of it, with Tavi's go-ahead for the hostname,
because the phone API keeps relying on Access (root CONTRACTS, `phone-api-one-account`). The
staging server's custom domain comes only from the `PULLY_STAGING_HOST` repository variable
(`scripts/staging-config.mjs`), which the operator sets after its Access application exists,
and the stable server's only from `PULLY_STABLE_HOST` (`scripts/stable-config.mjs`), set the
same way; `wrangler.jsonc` itself keeps no route. Source for staging: Tavi, 24 Oct 2026 20:46, a staging
app that updates when we merge to main. Only `/api/public/` and `/api/personal/` MAY bypass
Access, as they do in front of production's separate public listener: those routes refuse
Access credentials and cookies and answer only to their own GitHub sign-in (backend
`personal-public-read-is-a-typed-capability`, root `phone-api-one-account`).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] hosted-personal-in-its-own-object
Public browsing and personal GitHub sign-in and the personal workspace (`/api/public/`, `/api/personal/`,
`/workspace/`) MUST be answered
by the server's own `public_server` router in the `PersonalServer` Durable Object and the account
objects it hands requests to, never by `PullyServer`, as the native server answers them on a
separate listener with separate storage (backend `public-host-starts-before-legacy-authority`).
`PersonalServer` keeps the sign-in store in its SQLite and MUST NOT keep account data: its
factory for account stores refuses every account. Each personal account's reads and workspace
MUST be answered by that account's own `AccountServer` object, named by the backend's
`account_key`, whose stores are scopes of its own SQLite, so no account's object can read
another's records (backend `tenant-state-does-not-adopt-legacy-data`). Sign-in is the GitHub
CLI's device flow, and the vault keys come only from the `PULLY_PERSONAL_VAULT_KEYS` secret;
without it GitHub sign-in is reported as not configured. Source: Tavi, 25 Oct 2026, his server
agent's finding that Connect GitHub did not work on staging; one object per account from Tavi,
28 Oct 2026: "Why would we save anything to files instead of to the DO for each user? We have
proper user sepparation, no?"

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] hosted-account-object-acts-only-on-forwarded-grants
Only `PersonalServer` MAY reach an `AccountServer`: the Worker MUST NOT route any request to it.
`PersonalServer` resolves the caller's bearer through the vault (for `/workspace/`, as a
confirmed session) and forwards the request with that grant in `x-pully-grant`, replacing any
the caller sent; a bearer that does not resolve gets `PersonalServer`'s own refusal. The
account object MUST act only on a grant for its own account whose session hash is the request's
own bearer's, MUST send sign-out back to `PersonalServer`, and MUST get its background session
from `PersonalServer` each round. `PersonalServer` MUST tell the account object when a granted
session ends (sign-out, disconnect, expiry, a newer credential), and the account object MUST
then revoke what it holds for that credential revision, as the vault revokes captured
authority (backend `personal-session-is-bound-to-one-stable-user`); without a notice it MUST
revoke, at its next admission or background round, a credential not granted again for ten
minutes. Source: Tavi, 28 Oct 2026, one object
per account (`hosted-personal-in-its-own-object`).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] hosted-account-refreshes-its-own-pulls
Each `AccountServer` MUST refresh its account's open pull requests with the server's own
`warm_round` on its alarm, every `WARM_EVERY`, while the account has a confirmed session with
repository access, and MUST stop setting the alarm when it has none; a later request starts it
again. Source: Tavi, 28 Oct 2026, asking why stable is not on Workers and why only 150 pull
requests are refreshed.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] hosted-import-is-off-unless-its-token-is-set
The `/import/v1/` route that copies the VPS data in (`scripts/import-vps.mjs`) MUST answer 404
unless the `PULLY_IMPORT_TOKEN` secret is set, and then MUST answer only a POST carrying that
token, compared without early exit. It MUST NOT replace a record or analytics day the Worker
already has, except the sign-in store, which is copied whole; an account store MUST be written
only to the object of an account the copied sign-in store knows. Running it touches the VPS
data, so it waits for Tavi's go-ahead (coordinator relay, 28 Oct 2026: "switching the public
address and anything that touches the VPS data is a one-way door").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] hosted-stable-only-from-the-verified-release
The stable server MUST be deployed only by `.github/workflows/stable.yml`, as its own Worker
(`pully-stable`) with its own objects and Android bucket, from a release push whose CI passed
and that `scripts/release-track.mjs` admits (its `publication-needs-exact-verified-release`).
It MUST skip until `PULLY_STABLE_HOST` is set, which waits for Tavi's go-ahead to move that host
(`hosted-server-only-behind-access`). Source: Tavi, 28 Oct 2026: "Why does the stable server
not run on workers too? [...] We should be using Cloudflare for that too, no?"

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] hosted-data-in-durable-object-sqlite
The server's records MUST live in the `PullyServer` Durable Object's SQLite storage through
`SqlRecords`, split into parts below the 2 MB row limit, with each write made without an `await`
so its statements commit together (backend `rust-store-atomic-mutations`).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] hosted-secrets-named-not-forwarded
Only the variables named in `SERVER_ENVIRONMENT` (`src/lib.rs`) reach the server, and only when set
as Worker variables or secrets. Model provider API keys for Claude Code and Codex MUST NOT be
added to it (root CONTRACTS, `secrets-come-from-the-environment`; backend CONTRACTS,
`ai-runs-on-the-callers-own-sign-in`).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] hosted-analytics-in-durable-object-sqlite
Usage analytics MUST be kept in the `PullyServer` Durable Object's SQLite through `SqlDays`, one
row per event under its UTC day, as the Worker's form of the day files in root CONTRACTS
`analytics-stays-on-our-server`; the server's own `clean_event`, `PULLS_REVIEW_ANALYTICS=off` and
the 365-day limit apply unchanged (`analytics-what-not-how-much`, `analytics-can-be-turned-off`).
Events MUST be written as they arrive, with no timer, because a pending timer keeps the object
awake and billed (plans/12-hosted-server.md, M5).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] hosted-android-builds-in-r2
Published Android files MUST come from the `PULLY_ANDROID` R2 bucket under the same names as the
native server's Android directory, read through the server's own download routes, so the
download page, `latest.json` and its checks are the server's and not this crate's
(`hosted-server-is-the-rust-server-in-a-worker`). A response that states its length MUST keep
`Content-Length`, because the phone's update download shows its progress from it
(`android/core/.../DownloadUpdate.kt`). `scripts/upload-android.sh` MUST upload `latest.json`
last, so the manifest never names an APK the bucket lacks.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] hosted-ai-in-the-logins-own-container
Claude Code and Codex work for a login MUST run only in the container of that login's `AgentHome`
Durable Object, named after the login's volume, through the server's own agent code (`ai-kit/src/process.rs`)
run by the AI kit's runner, `ai-kit/src/runner.rs` (`hosted-server-is-the-rust-server-in-a-worker`). The object MUST refuse every
login but the first it served, and the runner MUST refuse every login but its container's. A
container MUST NOT be given a storage key, a server secret or another login's files. The object
keeps only that login's sign-in files, as text in its own storage: the runner gives the
sign-in part of each (Codex's tokens, Claude's OAuth login) and nothing else of the CLI home,
and the object writes them back when the container starts and saves them after each run,
sign-in, status check and sign-out. Inside the container, CLI jobs MUST run as a user that cannot read
the login homes (backend `rust-container-tools-use-scoped-capabilities`). Source: Tavi, 24 Oct
2026, "Move the server, AI last" and "Rewrite it as a Worker"; the login-storage question asked
the same day, answered by Tavi at 19:27 ("Can we not keep the logins in a D1 database? We
could just store them as text in there"), kept in each login's own object rather than one D1
database so no query can reach another login.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] hosted-staging-apk-validation
The staging publisher MUST verify the actual APK package, version and pinned signing key before
uploading anything. Multiple installed SDK build-tools versions MUST NOT change those checks;
missing required tools MUST fail before the build or upload. Source: Tavi, 24 Oct 2026, complete
staging after the first publication exposed the hosted runner's multiple SDK versions.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] hosted-personal-workspace-keeps-stable-owned-state-and-agent-remote
The account's `AccountServer` object MUST route /workspace/* through the backend's canonical
personal-session workspace router, and `PersonalServer` and `AccountServer` MUST each install
the own-login AgentHome remote even when PullyServer has never started in the isolate. Each
immutable personal account's saved tours, settings, reviews and analytics MUST survive object
restart in its own object's SQLite. Live jobs and private caches MUST remain captured-binding
state; a new binding MUST NOT adopt them. Workspace state and analytics MUST use records, never
wasm filesystem calls. No account MAY select another's store, job registry or CLI home.
Source: Tavi25Oct2026, full production workspace through one own GitHub app login; the
account's own object from Tavi, 28 Oct 2026 (`hosted-personal-in-its-own-object`).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] hosted-workspace-record-prefixes-use-scoped-ranges
ScopedRecords prefix lookups MUST constrain both the account scope and the literal encoded
id range before enumerating rows; SqlRecords MUST constrain the same literal id range.
Percent and underscore characters in encoded ids MUST NOT act as wildcards. Analytics
summary iteration MUST consume record batches or SQLite rows incrementally, with the
existing cleaner, Stats response and retention unchanged. Source: Tavi25Oct2026 review-fix
batch, finding 8; backend workspace-stats-reads-only-matching-records.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] hosted-workspace-discards-only-access-transport-cookies
Before forwarding /workspace/* to the backend, the Worker MUST discard the exact
CF_Authorization transport cookie and empty Cookie headers. Other cookies MUST remain
present for the backend's existing rejection, including mixed Access/application cookies
and malformed or lookalike cookie names. Authorization and every non-cookie header MUST
remain unchanged; public, personal sign-in, legacy and download cookie forwarding MUST
remain unchanged. No cookie MAY select an account or replace the confirmed personal
bearer, and no cookie value MAY be logged. Source: Tavi's 25 Oct 2026 one-GitHub-login
instruction and the staging service-auth request observed during PR127 live verification.
